            <ArticleTitle>[AXIN1-related CSRNP1 mRNA expression and its transcriptional regulation in TGF-ß1-induced tumor cells].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1122-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate AXIN1-related CSRNP1 gene expression and the mechanism of its transcriptional regulation in TGF-ß1-induced tumor cells.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Human lung carcinoma A549 cells or human prostate cancer PC3 cells were treated with TGF-ß1 at different doses (0, 20, 40, and 80 ng/ml) or at 20 ng/ml for 0, 8, 12, or 24 h, and the dose and time effect of TGF-ß1 on CSRNP1 mRNA expression in the tumor cells were evaluated with real-time RT-PCR. A549 cells were also treated with TGF-ß1 and cycloheximide to clarify whether CSRNP1 expression induced by TGF-ß1 required de novo protein synthesis. A549 cells transfected with pcDNA3.1, flag-SMAD3, or flag-SMAD3-mu, after serum starvation, were treated with or without TGF-ß1 (20 ng/mL) for 24 h, and the overexpression of wild-type SMAD3 and dominant negative SMAD3-mu mutant were confirmed by Western blotting. The effect of SMAD3 or SMAD3-mu overexpression on CSRNP1 mRNA expression was also measured by real-time RT-PCR.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In both A549 and PC3 cells, TGF-ß1 dose- and time-dependently stimulated CSRNP1 expression, which required de novo protein synthesis in A549 cells. Overexpression of wild-type SMAD3 significantly increased the expression of CSRNP1 mRNA induced by TGF-ß1, while overexpression of dominant negative SMAD3 mutant remarkably reduced CSRNP1 mRNA expression in response to TGF-ß1 in A549 cells.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">TGF-ß1 may contribute to CSRNP1 expression through SMAD3 activation and downstream signaling in tumor cells.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
